---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import LangToggle from '../../../components/LangToggle.astro';

// Qwen3.5-27B text_config (verified from HF Qwen/Qwen3.5-27B config.json, 2026-07-04):
// 64 layers, layer_types = 16 × [linear, linear, linear, full];
// full attention: 24 Q / 4 KV heads × head_dim 256, attn_output_gate, partial_rotary 0.25;
// linear (Gated DeltaNet): 16 K / 48 V heads × 128, conv kernel 4, mamba_ssm_dtype float32;
// hidden 5,120; FFN 17,408 dense (mlp_only_layers []); vocab 248,320; native ctx 262,144.
const NL = 64;
const layers = Array.from({ length: NL }, (_, i) => {
  const full = (i + 1) % 4 === 0; // indices 3, 7, …, 63 are full_attention
  const n = i + 1;
  return {
    i,
    full,
    tipEn: full
      ? `Layer ${n} — Gated Attention (full, GQA). 24 Q / 4 KV heads × 256; softmax over the whole prefix; KV cache +4 KB per token per layer — grows with T. Then dense SwiGLU FFN 5,120 → 17,408.`
      : `Layer ${n} — Gated DeltaNet (linear). q/k: 16 heads × 128, v: 48 heads × 128; recurrent state 48 × 128 × 128 fp32 ≈ 3 MB — constant in T. Then dense SwiGLU FFN 5,120 → 17,408.`,
    tipKo: full
      ? `Layer ${n} — Gated Attention (full, GQA). 24 Q / 4 KV heads × 256; 전체 prefix에 softmax; KV cache가 layer당 token마다 +4 KB — T에 비례해 증가. 이후 dense SwiGLU FFN 5,120 → 17,408.`
      : `Layer ${n} — Gated DeltaNet (linear). q/k 16 heads × 128, v 48 heads × 128; recurrent state 48 × 128 × 128 fp32 ≈ 3 MB — T와 무관하게 고정. 이후 dense SwiGLU FFN 5,120 → 17,408.`,
  };
});
---

<Base
  title="Hybrid attention anatomy: Qwen3.5 — Junwon Lee"
  description="Interactive tear-down of Qwen3.5's hybrid linear + full attention stack: the 3:1 Gated DeltaNet / Gated Attention interleave, both token mixers tensor by tensor, and the KV-cache-vs-recurrent-state memory race."
>
  <div class="hyb-page">
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="hero-top">
          <p class="eyebrow">Study · Model anatomy</p>
          <LangToggle />
        </div>
        <h1>
          <span class="lang-en">Inside Qwen3.5: a hybrid linear + full attention LLM</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">Qwen3.5 해부: linear + full attention 하이브리드 LLM</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="lede">
          <span class="lang-en">
            Qwen3.5 answers the KV-cache problem architecturally: three of every four layers
            replace softmax attention with a <em>Gated DeltaNet</em> whose memory is a fixed-size
            matrix, and the remaining fourth keeps full attention as random-access memory over the
            context. Walk the 64-layer interleave, open both token mixers, then race their memory
            footprints out to 262K tokens.
          </span>
          <span class="lang-ko">
            Qwen3.5는 KV cache 문제를 아키텍처로 푼다: 4개 layer 중 3개는 softmax attention을
            고정 크기 행렬 메모리를 갖는 <em>Gated DeltaNet</em>으로 대체하고, 나머지 1개는 컨텍스트
            전체를 임의 접근(random-access)할 수 있는 full attention으로 남겨 둔다. 64-layer
            인터리브를 훑고, 두 token mixer를 열어 본 뒤, 262K token까지 메모리 경주를 돌려 보자.
          </span>
        </p>

        <nav class="arc-roadmap" aria-label="Sections">
          <a href="#arc-s1"><span class="arc-n">§1</span><span class="lang-en">The itch</span><span class="lang-ko">문제</span></a>
          <a href="#arc-s2"><span class="arc-n">§2</span><span class="lang-en">Two memories</span><span class="lang-ko">두 가지 기억</span></a>
          <a href="#arc-s3"><span class="arc-n">§3</span><span class="lang-en">Layer stack</span><span class="lang-ko">레이어 스택</span></a>
          <a href="#arc-s4"><span class="arc-n">§4</span><span class="lang-en">Two mixers</span><span class="lang-ko">두 mixer</span></a>
          <a href="#arc-s5"><span class="arc-n">§5</span><span class="lang-en">Delta rule</span><span class="lang-ko">Delta rule</span></a>
          <a href="#arc-s6"><span class="arc-n">§6</span><span class="lang-en">Memory race</span><span class="lang-ko">메모리 경주</span></a>
          <a href="#arc-s7"><span class="arc-n">§7</span><span class="lang-en">The recall tax</span><span class="lang-ko">recall의 대가</span></a>
          <a href="#arc-s8"><span class="arc-n">§8</span><span class="lang-en">Where this goes</span><span class="lang-ko">다음 갈 곳</span></a>
        </nav>

        <div class="arc-prereq">
          <span class="lang-en">
            <strong>Before you start:</strong> this page assumes you can read a decoder block —
            what Q, K, V are, why decode-time inference keeps a <em>KV cache</em>, and roughly what
            RoPE does to Q and K. If any of that is hazy, the
            <a href="/study/models/attention-anatomy/">attention anatomy</a> page rebuilds standard
            attention tensor by tensor, and the <a href="/study/models/rope/">RoPE</a> page covers
            positional rotation. Everything else is introduced along the way.
          </span>
          <span class="lang-ko">
            <strong>시작 전에:</strong> 이 페이지는 decoder block을 읽을 수 있다는 전제로 쓰였다 —
            Q, K, V가 무엇인지, decode 추론이 왜 <em>KV cache</em>를 유지하는지, RoPE가 Q와 K에
            대략 무엇을 하는지. 흐릿하다면 <a href="/study/models/attention-anatomy/">attention
            해부</a> 페이지가 표준 attention을 tensor 단위로 다시 쌓아 주고,
            <a href="/study/models/rope/">RoPE</a> 페이지가 위치 회전을 다룬다. 나머지는 본문에서
            필요한 순간에 소개한다.
          </span>
        </div>

        <div class="config-note">
          <span class="config-lead">
            <span class="lang-en">Config on this page — Qwen3.5-27B (dense), read from the
            published <code>config.json</code> on 2026-07-04:</span>
            <span class="lang-ko">이 페이지의 config — Qwen3.5-27B (dense), 공개
            <code>config.json</code>에서 2026-07-04에 직접 확인:</span>
          </span>
          <span class="tag accent">64 layers = 16 × (3 linear + 1 full)</span>
          <span class="tag">d_model 5,120</span>
          <span class="tag">full: 24 Q / 4 KV heads × 256</span>
          <span class="tag">linear: 16 K / 48 V heads × 128</span>
          <span class="tag">FFN 17,408 (dense SwiGLU)</span>
          <span class="tag">vocab 248,320</span>
          <span class="tag accent">native ctx 262,144</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ §1 · THE ITCH ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="arc-s1">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="viz-h arc-heading">
          <span class="arc-num">§1</span>
          <span><span class="lang-en">The itch: memory that grows with every token</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">문제: token마다 자라는 메모리</span></span>
        </h2>
        <p class="arc-prose">
          <span class="lang-en">
            A decoder LLM generates one token at a time, and to attend back over its past it must
            <em>keep</em> that past: every attention layer appends the new token's K and V vectors
            to a cache, and nothing is ever evicted. The cost is small per token and merciless in
            aggregate. A conventional all-attention model of this page's shape pays 256 KB of cache
            per token; run it to Qwen3.5's native 262,144-token context and one sequence holds
            <strong>64 GB</strong> of cache — more than the 27B model's own BF16 weights (≈54 GB).
            Long context does not fail on compute first; it fails on memory. Batch sizes collapse,
            and the cost of a conversation scales with its length.
          </span>
          <span class="lang-ko">
            decoder LLM은 token을 하나씩 생성하고, 과거를 attend하려면 그 과거를 <em>보관</em>해야
            한다: 모든 attention layer가 새 token의 K, V 벡터를 cache에 덧붙이고, 무엇도 제거되지
            않는다. token당 비용은 작지만 누적은 무자비하다. 이 페이지와 같은 shape의 전통적
            all-attention 모델은 token당 cache 256 KB를 내는데, Qwen3.5의 네이티브 262,144-token
            context까지 돌리면 시퀀스 하나가 <strong>64 GB</strong>의 cache를 든다 — 27B 모델의
            BF16 가중치(≈54 GB)보다 크다. long context는 연산보다 메모리에서 먼저 무너진다.
            batch 크기가 붕괴하고, 대화 비용이 길이에 비례해 커진다.
          </span>
        </p>

        <div class="viz-frame">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 740 150" role="img" aria-label="The KV cache grows by 256 KB with every generated token; at 262,144 tokens it reaches 64 GB, larger than the model weights" style="width:100%; height:auto;">
            <text class="stitle" x="20" y="22">every generated token appends to every layer's cache — and nothing leaves</text>
            {Array.from({ length: 9 }, (_, i) => (
              <g>
                <rect class="sbox" x={20 + i * 52} y={38} width="40" height="22" rx="5"></rect>
                <text class="smono" x={40 + i * 52} y="53" text-anchor="middle">t{i + 1}</text>
                <rect class="itch-bar" x={24 + i * 52} y={104 - (i + 1) * 5} width="32" height={(i + 1) * 5} rx="2"></rect>
              </g>
            ))}
            <text class="smono" x="490" y="53">… t262,144</text>
            <rect class="itch-bar itch-bar-end" x="560" y="42" width="40" height="62" rx="3"></rect>
            <text class="stitle sm taccent" x="612" y="66">64 GB cache / sequence</text>
            <text class="ssub" x="612" y="84">at 256 KB per token × 262,144</text>
            <text class="smono" x="20" y="132">cache ledger: +256 KB / token (64 layers × 4 KB) — weights ≈ 54 GB stay fixed; the cache does not</text>
          </svg>
        </div>

        <div class="arc-takeaway">
          <span class="arc-takeaway-label"><span class="lang-en">Takeaway</span><span class="lang-ko">핵심 한 줄</span></span>
          <span class="lang-en">The KV cache is append-only state that grows without bound — at long
            context it, not the weights, is the resource that runs out.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">KV cache는 무한히 자라는 append-only state다 — long context에서
            바닥나는 자원은 가중치가 아니라 cache다.</span>
        </div>
        <p class="arc-question">
          <span class="lang-en">Can a layer mix the sequence without keeping the whole sequence around?</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">시퀀스 전체를 보관하지 않고도 layer가 시퀀스를 섞을 수 있을까?</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ §2 · FOUNDATIONS ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="arc-s2">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="viz-h arc-heading">
          <span class="arc-num">§2</span>
          <span><span class="lang-en">Foundations: two ways to remember a sequence</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">기초: 시퀀스를 기억하는 두 가지 방법</span></span>
        </h2>
        <p class="arc-prose">
          <span class="lang-en">
            First, be precise about what the cache buys. At decode time, softmax attention lets the
            current query score <em>every</em> stored key and read the matching values — token
            200,000 is as sharply addressable as token 3. It is a <strong>random-access
            archive</strong>: exact, position-addressable recall, paid for with O(T) memory and an
            O(T) read per token.
          </span>
          <span class="lang-ko">
            먼저 cache가 사 주는 것을 정확히 하자. decode 시점의 softmax attention은 현재 query가
            저장된 <em>모든</em> key를 채점하고 해당 value를 읽게 해 준다 — token 200,000도
            token 3만큼 선명하게 지정된다. 이것은 <strong>random-access 아카이브</strong>다:
            정확한 위치 지정 recall을, token당 O(T) 메모리와 O(T) 읽기로 사는 것이다.
          </span>
        </p>
        <p class="arc-prose">
          <span class="lang-en">
            The older alternative is the RNN's: fold history into a <strong>fixed-size state</strong>
            updated in place — O(1) memory, but the past survives only as a lossy summary. Linear
            attention connects the two worlds: drop the softmax, and the attention sum factors into
            a running matrix S = Σ v·kᵀ with output o = S·q — softmax attention's shape, an RNN's
            memory. But the plain version has two flaws: it never forgets (every write piles on top
            of the last), and it cannot <em>correct</em> — a new value for an old key just
            accumulates next to the stale one. Fixing those two flaws — a decay gate for forgetting,
            an error-correcting write for replacement — is exactly what "Gated" and "Delta" will
            mean in the mixer this page opens in §4.
          </span>
          <span class="lang-ko">
            더 오래된 대안은 RNN의 방식이다: 히스토리를 제자리에서 갱신되는 <strong>고정 크기
            state</strong>로 접어 넣는다 — O(1) 메모리, 대신 과거는 손실 요약으로만 남는다.
            linear attention이 두 세계를 잇는다: softmax를 빼면 attention 합이 누적 행렬
            S = Σ v·kᵀ로 인수분해되고 출력은 o = S·q — softmax attention의 형태에 RNN의 메모리다.
            그러나 순정 버전에는 결함이 둘 있다: 망각이 없고(모든 쓰기가 이전 위에 쌓인다),
            <em>수정</em>도 못 한다 — 같은 key의 새 value가 낡은 것 옆에 누적될 뿐이다. 이 두
            결함을 고치는 것 — 망각을 위한 decay gate, 교체를 위한 오차-수정 쓰기 — 이 바로 §4에서
            열어 볼 mixer의 "Gated"와 "Delta"의 의미다.
          </span>
        </p>

        <div class="viz-frame">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 740 190" role="img" aria-label="Two memory contracts: a growing archive of K V rows versus a fixed-size state matrix overwritten in place" style="width:100%; height:auto;">
            <text class="stitle taccent" x="60" y="24">archive — softmax attention</text>
            {Array.from({ length: 5 }, (_, i) => (
              <rect class="kv-chip" x="60" y={34 + i * 21} width="220" height="16" rx="4" opacity={1 - i * 0.13}></rect>
            ))}
            {Array.from({ length: 5 }, (_, i) => (
              <text class="smono" x="170" y={46 + i * 21} text-anchor="middle">K/V of token {i + 1}</text>
            ))}
            <text class="smono" x="170" y="152" text-anchor="middle">… one row per token, forever</text>
            <text class="ssub" x="170" y="174" text-anchor="middle">exact recall · O(T) memory</text>

            <text class="stitle tlin" x="450" y="24">slate — recurrent / linear state</text>
            <rect class="st-chip" x="450" y="34" width="110" height="104" rx="8"></rect>
            <text class="smono tlin" x="505" y="80" text-anchor="middle">S ∈ ℝ^(128×128)</text>
            <text class="smono" x="505" y="98" text-anchor="middle">overwritten in place</text>
            <path class="stateline" d="M596,60 C630,70 630,102 596,112"></path>
            <path d="M596,112 l10,-4 m-10,4 l9,5" class="stateline" style="stroke-dasharray:none;"></path>
            <text class="ssub" x="640" y="90">read + write,</text>
            <text class="ssub" x="640" y="104">every token</text>
            <text class="smono" x="505" y="152" text-anchor="middle">same size at token 1 and 262,144</text>
            <text class="ssub" x="505" y="174" text-anchor="middle">lossy summary · O(1) memory</text>
          </svg>
        </div>

        <div class="arc-takeaway">
          <span class="arc-takeaway-label"><span class="lang-en">Takeaway</span><span class="lang-ko">핵심 한 줄</span></span>
          <span class="lang-en">Sequence memory is a dial between an exact, growing archive and a
            lossy, constant slate — every long-context architecture is choosing a point on it.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">시퀀스 기억은 정확하지만 자라는 아카이브와 손실이 있지만 고정된
            슬레이트 사이의 다이얼이다 — 모든 long-context 아키텍처는 그 위의 한 점을 고른다.</span>
        </div>
        <p class="arc-question">
          <span class="lang-en">Qwen3.5 refuses to pick one end. Where, in its 64 layers, does it mix the two?</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">Qwen3.5는 한쪽 끝을 고르지 않는다. 64개 layer의 어디에서 둘을 섞을까?</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ §3 · LAYER-STACK MAP ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="stack-view">
      <div class="container" id="arc-s3">
        <p class="arc-bridge">
          <span class="lang-en">We now have the dial. Qwen3.5's position on it is written in a
            single config field — <code>layer_types</code> — and you can read the whole answer in
            one strip.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">이제 다이얼을 손에 들었다. Qwen3.5의 선택은 config의 필드 하나 —
            <code>layer_types</code> — 에 적혀 있고, 그 답 전체를 한 줄의 스트립으로 읽을 수 있다.</span>
        </p>
        <h2 class="viz-h arc-heading">
          <span class="arc-num">§3</span>
          <span><span class="lang-en">The layer stack: 48 linear + 16 full</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">레이어 스택: linear 48 + full 16</span></span>
        </h2>
        <p class="viz-sub">
          <span class="lang-en">The whole depth as one strip — exactly the
            <code>layer_types</code> list from the config. Hover any layer for its mixer and
            shapes; click to open the mixer internals below.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">모델 전체 깊이를 한 줄로 — config의 <code>layer_types</code>
            리스트 그대로다. layer에 hover하면 mixer 종류와 shape가 보이고, 클릭하면 아래
            mixer 내부로 이동한다.</span>
        </p>

        <div class="viz-frame">
          <div class="hyb-scroll">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 740 208" role="img" aria-label="Qwen3.5-27B layer stack: 64 layers, repeating 3 Gated DeltaNet then 1 Gated Attention, each followed by a dense SwiGLU FFN" style="width:100%; height:auto; min-width:720px;">
            <text class="stitle" x="20" y="20">layer_types — 16 × ( 3 × Gated DeltaNet → 1 × Gated Attention )</text>

            {layers.map((l) => (
              <a href="#mixer-view" class="cell-link" aria-label={`Layer ${l.i + 1}: ${l.full ? 'Gated Attention (full)' : 'Gated DeltaNet (linear)'}`}>
                <rect
                  class={`lcell ${l.full ? 'lc-full' : 'lc-lin'}`}
                  x={18 + l.i * 11} y="38" width="9" height="46" rx="2"
                  data-tip={l.tipEn} data-tip-ko={l.tipKo}
                ></rect>
              </a>
            ))}

            {[1, 16, 32, 48, 64].map((n) => (
              <text class="mlabel" x={18 + (n - 1) * 11 + 4.5} y="98" text-anchor="middle">{n}</text>
            ))}

            <!-- block braces every 4 layers -->
            {Array.from({ length: 16 }, (_, b) => (
              <rect x={18 + b * 44} y="86" width="42" height="2" rx="1" fill={b % 2 ? '#d1cfc5' : '#b9b7ad'}></rect>
            ))}

            <g data-tip="Every one of the 64 layers is followed by the same dense SwiGLU FFN: gate/up 5,120 → 17,408, down 17,408 → 5,120. mlp_only_layers is empty and there are no MoE params in the 27B config — the MoE variants live elsewhere in the family (e.g. Qwen3.5-397B-A17B)."
               data-tip-ko="64개 layer 전부 동일한 dense SwiGLU FFN이 뒤따른다: gate/up 5,120 → 17,408, down 17,408 → 5,120. 27B config에는 mlp_only_layers가 비어 있고 MoE 파라미터가 없다 — MoE는 패밀리의 다른 모델(예: Qwen3.5-397B-A17B) 몫이다.">
              <rect class="sbox sbox-warm" x="18" y="110" width="704" height="30" rx="7"></rect>
              <text class="ssub" x="370" y="129" text-anchor="middle">× 64 — dense SwiGLU FFN after every mixer: 5,120 → 17,408 → 5,120 (no MoE in the 27B config)</text>
            </g>

            <g transform="translate(18, 160)">
              <rect class="lcell lc-lin" x="0" y="0" width="12" height="12" rx="2"></rect>
              <text class="ssub" x="18" y="10">Gated DeltaNet (linear) × 48 — state 3 MB/layer, constant</text>
              <rect class="lcell lc-full" x="330" y="0" width="12" height="12" rx="2"></rect>
              <text class="ssub" x="348" y="10">Gated Attention (full, GQA) × 16 — KV +4 KB/token/layer</text>
            </g>
            <text class="smono" x="18" y="196">full_attention_interval: 4 → 75% of the stack never touches the KV cache</text>
          </svg>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="arc-prose">
          <span class="lang-en">
            The strip is the config's <code>layer_types</code> verbatim: 16 repeats of three Gated
            DeltaNet layers followed by one Gated Attention layer. Both mixers take [L × 5,120] in
            and give [L × 5,120] out, and both are followed by the identical dense SwiGLU FFN
            (5,120 → 17,408) — the residual stream cannot tell them apart. What differs is what each
            layer must <em>remember</em> to serve the next token: the full layer appends 4 KB of K/V
            per token and keeps it forever; the DeltaNet layer overwrites a fixed 3 MB matrix in place.
          </span>
          <span class="lang-ko">
            이 스트립은 config의 <code>layer_types</code> 그대로다: Gated DeltaNet 3개 + Gated
            Attention 1개가 16번 반복된다. 두 mixer 모두 [L × 5,120]을 받아 [L × 5,120]을 내놓고,
            뒤에는 동일한 dense SwiGLU FFN (5,120 → 17,408)이 붙는다 — residual stream 입장에서는
            구분이 안 된다. 다른 것은 다음 token을 위해 각 layer가 <em>기억해야 하는 것</em>이다:
            full layer는 token마다 4 KB의 K/V를 덧붙여 영원히 보관하고, DeltaNet layer는 고정된
            3 MB 행렬을 제자리에서 덮어쓴다.
          </span>
        </p>

