          <span class="lang-en">
            Per layer, the trade is 3,227,648 bytes of constant state (3 MB matrix + 80 KB conv
            buffer) against 4,096 bytes of KV per token — they tie at <strong>788 tokens</strong>.
            Everything past that is profit, and it compounds: at the native 262,144-token context
            the hybrid holds 16.1 GB where an all-full sibling would hold 64 GB. The asymptotic
            ratio is simply the layer ratio, 16/64 = 4×. Notice what the ratio does <em>not</em>
            change: the 16 full layers still grow linearly. The hybrid divides the KV-cache
            problem by four; it does not delete it.
